Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:50:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ieframe: InternetExplorer.Application Document, ReadyState,
 geometry, properties and bars (3013)

The InternetExplorer object (the top-level browser window created by
CreateObject("InternetExplorer.Application")) left most of IWebBrowser2
unimplemented: Document, ReadyState, LocationName, Left/Top/Width/Height,
Name, FullName, Path, Quit, PutProperty/GetProperty, ClientToWindow, ExecWB
and QueryStatusWB, and the bar and mode flags all returned E_NOTIMPL.
Scripts that drive Internet Explorer through automation need these.

- Document returns the HTML document, ReadyState the document state,
  LocationName the title (or the URL), Application and Parent the object itself,
  TopLevelContainer is true.
- Left, Top, Width and Height read and set the frame window rectangle;
  ClientToWindow adds the non-client size.
- Name, FullName and Path describe iexplore.exe.
- PutProperty and GetProperty keep a per-window case-insensitive property bag.
- StatusBar, ToolBar, AddressBar, TheaterMode and FullScreen keep their state and
  fire the corresponding events; the status bar is shown or hidden and the
  document area laid out again; StatusText reads the status bar text; MenuBar
  reports the menu.
- Offline, Silent, RegisterAsBrowser, RegisterAsDropTarget and Resizable keep
  their value.
- ExecWB and QueryStatusWB go to the document's command target.
- Quit closes the frame window.

